<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Direct and inverse by the unitary method</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) A posho mill grinds \({@G@}\) kg of maize in \({@t@}\) hours. Working at the same rate, how long does it take to grind \({@G2@}\) kg?</p><p>[[input:ans1]] hours [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</p><p>(b) \({@w@}\) workers can weed a shamba in \({@d@}\) days. How many days would \({@w2@}\) workers take, working at the same rate?</p><p>[[input:ans2]] days [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</p><p>Give each answer exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) More maize takes more time: this is direct proportion, so the ratio of time to mass stays the same.</p><p>\({@G@}\) kg take \({@t@}\) hours.<br/>1 kg takes \(\dfrac{ {@t@} }{ {@G@} }\) hours.<br/>\({@G2@}\) kg take \(\dfrac{ {@t@} }{ {@G@} } \times {@G2@} = {@dd(A)@}\) hours.</p><p>(b) More workers finish sooner: this is inverse proportion, so the product of workers and days stays the same.</p><p>\({@w@}\) workers take \({@d@}\) days.<br/>1 worker takes \({@w@} \times {@d@} = {@wd@}\) days.<br/>\({@w2@}\) workers take \({@wd@} \div {@w2@} = {@dd(Dd)@}\) days.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
